TOKEN tinybird_read READ

DESCRIPTION >
What D1 was doing around a moment: per second, per service, route and query
shape, the calls started, their summed and longest wall time, D1's own SQL
time, rows read and failures. Pass `at` (UTC, e.g. 2026-11-23 13:02:06) and
optionally `before_seconds` (default 60) and `after_seconds` (default 10).
The culprit shows up before the stall; the stall shows as long durations and
failures on the victims.

NODE d1_stall_context_seconds
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        toStartOfSecond(timestamp) AS second,
        service,
        route_path,
        method,
        cityHash64(sql) AS sql_hash,
        any(substring(sql, 1, 300)) AS sql_sample,
        count() AS calls,
        sum(duration_ms) AS total_ms,
        max(duration_ms) AS max_ms,
        round(sum(ifNull(sql_duration_ms, 0)), 1) AS sql_ms,
        sum(ifNull(rows_read, 0)) AS rows_read,
        sum(ifNull(rows_written, 0)) AS rows_written,
        countIf(error_code != '') AS failed,
        groupUniqArrayIf(error_code, error_code != '') AS error_codes
    FROM d1_call_event
    WHERE environment = {{ String(environment, 'production') }}
        AND timestamp >= toDateTime64({{ String(at, '2026-11-23 13:02:06', required=True) }}, 3, 'UTC')
            - toIntervalSecond({{ UInt32(before_seconds, 60) }})
        AND timestamp < toDateTime64({{ String(at, '2026-11-23 13:02:06', required=True) }}, 3, 'UTC')
            + toIntervalSecond({{ UInt32(after_seconds, 10) }})
    GROUP BY second, service, route_path, method, sql_hash
    ORDER BY second, total_ms DESC

TYPE endpoint
